{#-
  VideoControls (SPEC §9.2, §9.3, §12; HANDOFF §5 FormatLinks, StarRating):
  the one row of controls right after every video.

    {% from "partials/video-controls.njk" import videoControls %}
    {{ videoControls(video, site.features.ratings === true) }}
    {{ videoControls(video, ratingsOn, 'solution__tools') }}

  Arguments:
    video    a video from `videoById` (or `introChapters`/`solutionsByTier`)
    ratings  exactly true: the ratings widget ends the row
             (partials/rating.njk; the callers pass
             site.features.ratings === true)
    classes  extra classes for the row (a page's own placement)

  In this order, each only if the video has it:
  - Audio only: a native <details> holding <audio controls preload="none">
    (the video's own soundtrack, SPEC §9.2). First, so opening it never
    moves its own button: open, it takes the row's full width
    (components.css), the player opens under its button, and the handout
    and the stars move down under the player.
  - Handout: a link to the PDF in media/pdf/. Every video is to have one
    (SPEC §9.3), and it is the video's text alternative: it carries the full
    narration (there are no transcripts on the site). Its format is still
    open (PDF, Word or web page, SPEC §9.3, §21), so the label is "Handout"
    and the format is said only to screen readers. It is the only handout
    link near the video: the page's YouTube note doesn't repeat it.
  - "Was this helpful?" and the five stars, then the rating's status line on
    its own line under the row.

  One row where there is room, wrapping where there isn't (components.css).
  With nothing to show, nothing renders. A row holding only the ratings
  widget ships `hidden data-rating-reveal`, as the widget does, so nothing
  shows without JavaScript; rating.js reveals both.

  Without JavaScript the handout and audio work as they are. src/js/players.js
  pauses other media when audio plays and has the event hooks (data-handout
  and the audio's data-media hold the video_id, whatever the handout's
  format or the audio's file name; SPEC §9.4, §10.2). pages.json reads the
  same attributes (SPEC §8.3), so the Worker accepts exactly these ids.

  ids: audio-<video_id>, and the widget's rating-<video_id>-*. The validator
  allows each video once per page, so they are unique.
-#}
{%- from "partials/icons.njk" import icon -%}
{%- from "partials/rating.njk" import rating -%}
{%- macro videoControls(video, ratings=false, classes='') -%}
{%- set ratingsOn = ratings === true -%}
{%- set hasFormats = video.handout or video.audio -%}
{%- if hasFormats or ratingsOn %}
<div class="video-controls{% if classes %} {{ classes }}{% endif %}"{% if not hasFormats %} hidden data-rating-reveal{% endif %}>
  {%- if video.audio %}
  <details class="format-disclosure" id="audio-{{ video.video_id }}">
    <summary class="format-disclosure__toggle"><span class="format-button">{{ icon('headphones', 18, 'format-button__icon') }}Audio only<span class="visually-hidden">: {{ video.title }}</span>{{ icon('chevron-down', 16, 'format-disclosure__chevron') }}</span></summary>
    <div class="format-disclosure__panel">
      <audio class="format-audio" controls preload="none" src="/media/audio/{{ video.audio }}" data-media="{{ video.video_id }}" aria-label="Audio only: {{ video.title }}"><a href="/media/audio/{{ video.audio }}">Download the audio (MP3)</a></audio>
    </div>
  </details>
  {%- endif %}
  {%- if video.handout %}
  <a class="format-button" href="/media/pdf/{{ video.handout }}" type="application/pdf" data-handout="{{ video.video_id }}">{{ icon('download', 18, 'format-button__icon') }}Handout<span class="visually-hidden">: {{ video.title }} (PDF)</span></a>
  {%- endif %}
  {%- if ratingsOn %}
  {{ rating(video) }}
  {%- endif %}
</div>
{%- endif %}
{%- endmacro -%}
